RED record: Cycle 002 audit accepts a nonexistent referenced log
==================================================================
Date: 2026-08-15
Pre-fix artifact: git blob b869852a (scripts/ms05_evidence_audit.py, Cycle 002)

Demonstration: a commands.txt references logs/build.log, but the file does
not exist on disk. The old audit_commands only verifies referenced logs whose
basename is ALREADY in the discovered raw_log_names set:

    for ref in re.finditer(r"(\S+\.log)", commands_text):
        name = ref.group(1)
        if name in raw_log_names:          # <-- skip when basename absent
            target = log_root / name
            if not target.exists() or ...:
                raise AuditFailure(...)

A referenced log whose basename is not in the discovered set is silently
skipped. The old audit therefore accepts the missing log.

Result: OLD AUDIT: ACCEPTED missing referenced log -> RED CONFIRMED
New validator: returns MISSING_LOG for the same fixture.
